WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.990
You're deep into an essay.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.370
Then someone trips over the plug.

3
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.110
The screen goes black.

4
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.350
Power back on, and the essay has vanished.

5
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.910
Yet the computer starts itself
up and shows its start-up screen,

6
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.690
as if nothing happened.

7
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.030
So if it forgot your essay, how
did it remember how to start?

8
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.670
Did it download its start-up steps?

9
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.490
In this mission, you'll
meet primary storage,

10
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.650
the memory the CPU can access directly.

11
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.250
You'll find that some memory loses
everything when the power goes.

12
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.910
And that some memory keeps its contents,
even when the computer is unplugged.

13
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.970
Your mission: explain how a computer that
loses your essay can still start itself

14
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:41.360
up.
